# Read only by a build whose context is the repository's root -- and no build
# of this project is one. Each image is built from its own directory
# (`apps/api`, `apps/api-nest`, `apps/web`), and Docker takes the ignore file
# from the root of the context: `apps/api/.dockerignore` and its two siblings
# are the files that decide what an image is built from. This one stood alone
# until 2026-10-08 and protected nothing (D240 in docs/roadmap.md). It is kept
# for the day something is built from here.

.git
.github
.gitignore
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/out
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.venv
**/venv
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/htmlcov
**/.coverage
**/coverage.xml
**/*.sqlite3
apps/api/staticfiles
apps/api/media
apps/api/logs
apps/web/test-results
apps/web/playwright-report
docs
backups
